# data/

DrWatson's data directory, bound per machine (VisualGeometryToolkitEval Experiments):

| Tree | Resolved by | Access |
|---|---|---|
| `data_root()` — inputs | `VGTK_DATA_ROOT`, else `data/exp_raw` (a link or a directory), else the site profile's `data_root` (`VGTK_SITE`), else the artifact view of the published data (`configs/data_artifacts.toml`, `scripts/fetch_data.jl`) | read-only: a driver never writes here (`assert_not_input`) |
| `results_root()` — results | `VGTK_RESULTS_ROOT`, else `data/exp_pro`, else the site profile's `results_root` | add-only: one directory per run key, each with `_config.toml` and `_provenance.toml` |
| `datadir("sims")` | — | smoke runs, never read by a paper asset |

`data/exp_raw`, `data/exp_pro` and `data/sims` are ignored by git, and
nothing under `data/` but this file is tracked. Configs name inputs relative to
`data_root()` (an `[inputs.<id>]` names its catalogued `tier`); no code, test,
config or doc names a machine path: a machine's paths live in
VisualGeometryToolkitEval's site profiles (`configs/sites/`, selected by
`VGTK_SITE`), and the published inputs' bytes in the artifact store
(`VGTK_ARTIFACT_STORE`, or the site's `[storage] artifact_store`), never in the
Julia depot. `julia --project=. scripts/fetch_data.jl` installs them and links
them into `data/exp_raw`.
